"notre-dame":[
["Why is it called The Hunchback of Notre-Dame in English?","The title comes from Frederic Shoberl's 1833 translation; Hugo's own title puts the cathedral, not Quasimodo, at the centre."],
["What is the word 'Ananke'?","Hugo says he found the Greek word for 'fate' or 'necessity' carved in a dark corner of the cathedral and built the novel around it."],
["When is the novel set?","In Paris in 1482, under Louis XI, who appears in person in the Bastille counting his money."],
["Why is Quasimodo called that?","Frollo found the foundling on Quasimodo Sunday, after Easter, named from the Latin 'Quasi modo geniti infantes' ('like newborn babes'), and 'quasimodo' also means 'almost'."],
["Who is Esmeralda really?","She is Agnès, the stolen baby of the recluse Paquette, or Sister Gudule, who recognizes her by a tiny embroidered shoe just before the soldiers drag her to the gallows."],
["How does it end?","Esmeralda is hanged, Quasimodo throws Frollo from the tower, and years later two skeletons are found entwined in the Montfaucon vault, the hunchback's crumbling to dust when separated."],
["What does 'This will kill that' mean?","In the chapter 'Ceci tuera cela', Frollo, pointing from a printed book to the cathedral, predicts that printing will kill architecture as humanity's great way of recording ideas."],
["Who is Phoebus?","Captain Phoebus de Châteaupers, the vain officer Esmeralda loves; Frollo stabs him at their rendezvous, Esmeralda is blamed, and Phoebus survives to marry Fleur-de-Lys."],
["What does Djali the goat do?","Esmeralda's goat spells 'Phoebus' with letter blocks, a trick that helps convict her of witchcraft."],
["Did the novel save the cathedral?","Its success fed the campaign that led to the restoration by Lassus and Viollet-le-Duc from 1844, which added the spire and the famous chimeras."],
["How did Hugo make his deadline?","His wife Adèle recalled that he locked away his clothes so he couldn't go out, wrapping himself in a grey shawl to finish by early 1831."],
["What happened after the 2019 fire?","The fire destroyed the spire and roof, the novel shot to the top of French bestseller lists, and the restored cathedral reopened in December 2024."],
["How do the films change the story?","Disney's 1996 film lets Quasimodo live and makes Frollo a judge; the 1939 Hollywood version starred Charles Laughton as Quasimodo."]
],
